<h2>2. Purpose</h2>
<p>These terms govern the use of Signoff ("Signoff", "we"), an online service that lets a freelancer submit deliverables or project stages to their client, collect the client's approval or change requests, and keep a timestamped history. They apply as soon as an account is created. The service is intended for professionals acting in the course of their business.</p>
<p>A freelancer's client who opens an approval page is also bound by sections 6 and 8. When approving, the page tells the client: "<%= t('review.decision.intro') %>"</p>

<h2>3. What Signoff is, and what it is not</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Signoff provides a timestamped history and a digital fingerprint (SHA-256) of the files, which can serve as an element of proof of an agreement between the freelancer and their client. On approval, Signoff records the full name typed by the client, the date and time (UTC), their IP address, their browser and a frozen copy of the deliverables, and produces an approval certificate.</li>
  <li>Signoff does not verify the identity of the person who uses the link. The history is not a qualified electronic signature within the meaning of Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 ("eIDAS"), nor an advanced form of one, and does not replace a written contract. In a dispute, it is for the judge to assess this history together with the other evidence.</li>
  <li>Signoff is not a party to the relationship between the freelancer and their client: it does not answer for the quality of the work, the payment or the performance of the contract between them, and gives no legal advice.</li>
  <li>Signoff is not a payment service and collects no money on the freelancer's behalf.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Account and access</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Sign-up is currently by invitation (invitation code).</li>
  <li>You provide accurate information, keep your password confidential and are responsible for the activity of your account. Tell us at <%- legal('contactEmail') %> if there is any unauthorised access.</li>
  <li>You declare that you use the service in the course of your professional activity.</li>
  <li>One account per person. You can delete it at any time from "My profile" (password and confirmation word required). Deletion erases the account, the projects, the milestones or deliveries with their deliverables, the files, the notes, the supplements and the logs, including what was already approved and locked; links sent to clients stop working. The details, including the storage cleanup and the expiry of backups, are in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</li>
<% if (beta) { %>
  <li>When signing up, you accept the beta rules (checkbox); the date of this acceptance is recorded.</li>
  <li>If you forget your password during the beta, while sending emails is not turned on, an administrator resets it and sends you a link valid for 24 hours.</li>
<% } %>
</ul>

<% if (beta) { %>
